        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Rain rattled harder beyond the wide workshop gate. Mert still occupied the approach, keeping the safety boundary active, while Aya faced him across the same restored mosaic panel.\n\n“Lift on three,” Mert said. “Keep your side level.”\n\nAya almost answered that she knew. Instead, she planted her feet and watched his hands settle against his side of the panel.\n\n“One,” he counted.\n\nThe strengthening wind drove rain across the yard outside.\n\n“Two.”\n\nAya checked that her hold matched his.\n\n“Three.”\n\nAya and Mert lifted the mosaic panel together. Its full weight came into their shared hold, one carrier on each side. The restored surface stayed level between them, fragile but intact.\n\nAya’s first impulse was to move at once. She stopped herself. Mert adjusted his stance without loosening his side, and she followed the small correction so the panel did not tilt.\n\n“Steady,” he said.\n\n“Steady,” Aya agreed.\n\nOnly then did Mert release the gate boundary. Still supporting the panel with Aya, he shifted his body out of the gate’s blocked approach and opened the way ahead.\n\nAya saw him make that change. She saw the clear approach beyond him and understood that the boundary was no longer active.\n\nShe did not rush toward it.\n\n“We have the hold,” she said, keeping her eyes on the panel’s level edge.\n\nMert gave a brief nod. Together they remained inside the workshop, holding the same intact panel securely while rain drummed over the covered route ahead.",
